{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SVz58ngnpMvJTnb47c3KkC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Specs live in `docs/`, implementations in `cmd/`, shared libraries in `pkg/` (sys, format, testutils). Differential testing harness compares Go binary output against GNU reference binary byte-for-byte.\n\n**Current state:** Releases 00.0 through 02.2 are implemented (code at generation tags). Releases 03.0–04.1 have specs written. Release 05.0 (echo, tac, nl, fold) is `spec_complete` with code `not started` — this is the target.\n\n**Priority:** Release 05.0 — text stream transforms. Four use cases: echo, tac, nl, fold. All spec_complete, none started. Echo is the simplest and alphabetically first, making it the canonical first task.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\nPer constraints: 1 task max, implementation only (tests separate), anchored to PRD requirements.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/echo: implement echo utility (prd-echo R1-R4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd010-echo.yaml (all requirements and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.0-uc001-echo.yaml (end-to-end execution path)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.0.yaml (echo test cases for differential testing)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- differential testing pattern, SIGPIPE handling)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n      - cmd/true/main.go (reference for trivial utility structure)\n      - cmd/basename/main.go (reference for argument-processing utility structure)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/echo/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: echo command implementation with flag parsing and escape sequence handling\n      - path: cmd/echo/echo_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gecho reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement echo that prints all arguments separated by single spaces, followed by a newline, to stdout. With no arguments, print only a newline.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement -n flag: suppress the trailing newline.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement -e flag: enable interpretation of backslash escape sequences (\\\\\\\\, \\\\a, \\\\b, \\\\c, \\\\e, \\\\f, \\\\n, \\\\r, \\\\t, \\\\v, \\\\0NNN octal, \\\\xHH hex). \\\\c stops output immediately (no trailing newline, no further characters).\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement -E flag (default): disable interpretation of backslash escapes. When neither -e nor -E is given, behave as -E. Echo always exits 0 unless a write error occurs.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per the shared SIGPIPE protocol in ARCHITECTURE.yaml.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use manual flag parsing, not flag package. GNU echo treats --help and --version as literal arguments (not flags) when mixed with other args. Only recognize -n, -e, -E as flags, and only when they appear as leading arguments before non-flag arguments.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Match GNU echo flag clustering behavior: -neE and -en are valid combined flags. Stop flag parsing at the first non-flag argument.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Differential tests use gecho as the reference binary. Skip with t.Skip if gecho is not in PATH per the graceful-skip protocol.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/echo/main.go compiles with no errors and no golangci-lint warnings.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/echo/ passes. Differential tests compare Go echo against gecho for: no args, simple args, -n flag, -e with each escape sequence, -E with backslash literals, -e with \\\\c, combined -ne, and arguments that look like flags after a non-flag arg.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Echo exits 0 on success. SIGPIPE handler installed.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"No imports of external packages beyond standard library and pkg/sys. No imports of any cmd/ or other pkg/ package.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27540,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27540},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79a989b0-80ee-4ea3-a97c-56d74f843717","uuid":"9e649bb7-b8a7-4737-a073-1db61272d08a"}
